  "title": "Ratio test with factorials",
  "prompt": "Does $\\displaystyle \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{3^n}{n!}$ converge or diverge?",
  "answer_format": "'converges' or 'diverges' (add 'absolutely' or 'conditionally' when the terms change sign).",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "tags": [
    "ratio test",
    "factorials"
  ],
  "data": {
    "term": "3^n/n!"
  },
  "answer": "converges",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "Factorials suggest the ratio test.",
    "(n+1)! = (n+1)·n!, so most of the ratio cancels."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "$\\left|\\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}\\right| = \\frac{3^{n+1}}{(n+1)!}\\cdot\\frac{n!}{3^n} = \\frac{3}{n+1} \\to 0$.",
    "$L = 0 < 1$, so the series converges (absolutely)."
  ],
  "reference": {
    "book": "openstax-calc2",
    "section": "5.6 Ratio and Root Tests",
    "note": "Original problem."
  },
